{#-
  DeepSeek-V4-Flash chat template.

  DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 ships no `chat_template` in tokenizer_config.json: it
  builds prompts with the Python encoder in the base repository's `encoding/`
  directory instead. This file reproduces `encode_messages()` from that encoder
  so the checkpoint can be served through any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The
  encoder itself is shipped alongside, in `encoding/encoding_dsv4.py`, and is
  the authority whenever the two disagree.

  THINKING IS THE DEFAULT here. The encoder takes `thinking_mode` as a required
  argument with no default; this template picks one, and picks the same mode the
  base model is normally used in.

      apply_chat_template(msgs, add_generation_prompt=True)                     -> thinking
      apply_chat_template(msgs, add_generation_prompt=True, enable_thinking=False)

      # SGLang / llama-server, per request:
      {"messages": [...], "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}

  `reasoning_effort` is "low" (the encoder's default), "high" or "max". It is
  only ever a block of text prepended to the whole prompt, and only in thinking
  mode -- see REASONING_EFFORT_PROMPTS in encoding_dsv4.py.

  **The published benchmark numbers for this checkpoint were measured with
  enable_thinking=false.** They are a measure of what expert compression cost,
  not a claim about this default.

  Tool calling: `tools` arrives the standard OpenAI/llama-server way (a
  top-level render kwarg), `role: "tool"` messages carry results, and assistant
  `tool_calls` are OpenAI-shaped. The encoder itself has no top-level `tools`
  kwarg or standalone `tool` role -- callers attach `tools` to a message (by
  convention, the system message) and run merge_tool_messages() first (folds
  `tool` messages into the preceding user turn as `<tool_result>` blocks). This
  template reproduces that composition inline: `tools` is spliced onto the
  first system message's content (or, if there is no system message, rendered
  on its own at the very start -- equivalent to encode_messages() being called
  with a synthetic empty system message carrying `tools`). Whenever `tools` is
  supplied, encode_messages() stops dropping earlier reasoning_content
  (effective_drop_thinking=False) -- ported below as `has_tools`.

  Six details that are easy to get wrong, all verified against the encoder:

  * The assistant marker is a *transition* emitted at the end of a user turn
    (encoding_dsv4.py:381-407), not at the start of the assistant turn. The
    encoder has no `add_generation_prompt` concept -- it always emits this
    transition when the next message is an assistant turn, or when the user
    turn is the last one. This template does gate the *last-message* case on
    it (`(loop.last and add_generation_prompt) or (not loop.last and ...)`),
    purely so llama.cpp's server can auto-derive `generation_prompt` --
    it renders the template once with and once without that flag and diffs
    the two outputs, which only works if they can actually differ. Without
    this gate both renders are byte-identical (the encoder ignores the flag
    entirely), the diff comes out empty, and the DeepSeek V3.2/V4 specialized
    response parser silently loses the `<｜Assistant｜>` prefix it expects,
    rejecting every completion -- not just tool calls, *any* completion, with
    "The model produced output that does not match the expected peg-native
    format". Every real call from this template still passes
    `add_generation_prompt=True`, so this is a no-op for actual generation.
  * In thinking mode that marker is followed by `<think>`, and in chat mode by
    `</think>` -- the thinking *end* token, which closes the block before the
    model can open it. Only the final turn opens a block: earlier user turns get
    `</think>` even in thinking mode (:402-406) -- unless `tools` were supplied
    anywhere, in which case every turn opens `<think>` (drop_thinking is forced
    off).
  * `drop_thinking` defaults to True, so `reasoning_content` on assistant turns
    at or before the last user message is dropped (:359-363) -- again, unless
    `tools` were supplied.
  * Consecutive user messages, and any run of user/tool messages, are merged
    into one `<｜User｜>` block joined by a blank line, by merge_tool_messages()
    before rendering; a `tool` message renders as
    `<tool_result>...</tool_result>`.
  * `func['arguments']` in `tool_calls` may already be a dict for some clients;
    parse it with `from_json` only when it's a string, matching
    `encode_arguments_to_dsml`'s `json.loads`.
  * Tool schema / non-string argument JSON goes through the `tojson` filter,
    which must be registered to match `to_json()`
    (`json.dumps(v, ensure_ascii=False)`, insertion order preserved) rather
    than a stock htmlsafe/sort_keys `tojson` -- the renderer embedding this
    template is responsible for that; `verify_chat_template.py` does it for
    local checks.

  Not implemented: `latest_reminder`, `developer`, the internal task tokens,
  `response_format`, `context`, and reordering out-of-order parallel tool
  results to match call order (`sort_tool_results_by_call_order` in the
  encoder) -- this template assumes tool results arrive in the same order the
  tool calls were issued, which holds for every OpenAI-compatible client we've
  seen. Use the bundled encoder if you need any of these.
-#}
{%- set thinking = enable_thinking if enable_thinking is defined else true -%}
{%- set effort = reasoning_effort if reasoning_effort is defined else 'low' -%}
{%- set effort_prompts = {
    'low': '',
    'high': 'Reasoning Effort: Absolute maximum with no shortcuts permitted.\nYou MUST be very thorough in your thinking and comprehensively decompose the problem to resolve the root cause, rigorously stress-testing your logic against all potential paths, edge cases, and adversarial scenarios.\nExplicitly write out your entire deliberation process, documenting every intermediate step, considered alternative, and rejected hypothesis to ensure absolutely no assumption is left unchecked.\n\n',
    'max': 'Reasoning Effort: Beyond maximum — exhaustive, relentless, and uncompromising.\nYou MUST reason with the utmost depth and rigor, leaving absolutely nothing to chance: exhaustively decompose the problem into its most fundamental components, trace every causal chain to its root, and resolve the underlying cause rather than any surface symptom.\nDo not stop reasoning until you have independently verified the solution from multiple angles and are certain that no assumption remains unchecked and no error remains undiscovered.\n\n'
} -%}
{%- if effort not in effort_prompts -%}
    {{- raise_exception('deepseek-v4 chat template: reasoning_effort must be low, high or max, got ' + effort) -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set has_tools = tools is defined and tools -%}
{#- dsml_token as a named variable (not just an inlined literal) is what makes
    llama.cpp's server recognize this as a DeepSeek V3.2/V4-family template
    (common_chat_try_specialized_template in common/chat.cpp: it string-matches
    "dsml_token" + "DSML" + "tool_calls" in the template source) and hand tool
    call *parsing* off to its own hardened PEG grammar instead of trying to
    auto-generate one by executing this template's tool-call-rendering branch
    with synthetic data -- which would otherwise fail: this llama.cpp build's
    Jinja engine (common/jinja/value.cpp) implements `tojson` but not
    `from_json`, so the defensive `args | from_json` fallback below can never
    actually run standalone. It's still safe to keep: llama.cpp pre-parses any
    string-typed `tool_calls[].function.arguments` into a real object before
    handing messages to this template whenever its capability probe sees the
    template access fields on a native-object argument successfully (which
    ours does), so `from_json` is dead code on that server -- but any other
    OpenAI-compatible frontend that renders this template directly, without
    that pre-parse, needs it. -#}
{%- set dsml_token = '｜DSML｜' -%}
{%- set tools_header = '## Tools\n\nYou have access to a set of tools to help answer the user\'s question. You can invoke tools by writing a "<' + dsml_token + 'tool_calls>" block like the following:\n\n<' + dsml_token + 'tool_calls>\n<' + dsml_token + 'invoke name="$TOOL_NAME">\n<' + dsml_token + 'parameter name="$PARAMETER_NAME" string="true|false">$PARAMETER_VALUE</' + dsml_token + 'parameter>\n...\n</' + dsml_token + 'invoke>\n<' + dsml_token + 'invoke name="$TOOL_NAME2">\n...\n</' + dsml_token + 'invoke>\n</' + dsml_token + 'tool_calls>\n\nString parameters should be specified as is and set `string="true"`. For all other types (numbers, booleans, arrays, objects), pass the value in JSON format and set `string="false"`.\n\nIf thinking_mode is enabled (triggered by <think>), you MUST output your complete reasoning inside <think>...</think> BEFORE any tool calls or final response.\n\nOtherwise, output directly after </think> with tool calls or final response.\n\n### Available Tool Schemas\n\n' -%}
{%- set tools_footer = '\n\nYou MUST strictly follow the above defined tool name and parameter schemas to invoke tool calls.\n' -%}
{%- set tools_block = '' -%}
{%- if has_tools -%}
    {%- set ts = namespace(schemas=[]) -%}
    {%- for tool in tools -%}
        {%- set _ = ts.schemas.append(tool['function'] | tojson) -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- set tools_block = tools_header + (ts.schemas | join('\n')) + tools_footer -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{- '<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- set ns = namespace(last_user = -1, has_system = false, tools_rendered = false) -%}
{%- for message in messages -%}
    {%- if message['role'] == 'user' or message['role'] == 'tool' -%}
        {%- set ns.last_user = loop.index0 -%}
    {%- elif message['role'] == 'system' -%}
        {%- set ns.has_system = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if thinking -%}
    {{- effort_prompts[effort] -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if has_tools and not ns.has_system -%}
    {{- '\n\n' + tools_block -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- for message in messages -%}
    {%- if message['role'] == 'system' -%}
        {{- message['content'] -}}
        {%- if has_tools and not ns.tools_rendered -%}
            {{- '\n\n' + tools_block -}}
            {%- set ns.tools_rendered = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- elif message['role'] == 'user' or message['role'] == 'tool' -%}
        {%- if loop.index0 > 0 and (messages[loop.index0 - 1]['role'] == 'user' or messages[loop.index0 - 1]['role'] == 'tool') -%}
            {{- '\n\n' -}}
        {%- else -%}
            {{- '<｜User｜>' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if message['role'] == 'tool' -%}
            {{- '<tool_result>' + (message['content'] or '') + '</tool_result>' -}}
        {%- else -%}
            {{- message['content'] or '' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if (loop.last and add_generation_prompt) or (not loop.last and messages[loop.index0 + 1]['role'] == 'assistant') -%}
            {{- '<｜Assistant｜>' -}}
            {%- if thinking and (has_tools or loop.index0 >= ns.last_user) -%}
                {{- '<think>' -}}
            {%- else -%}
                {{- '</think>' -}}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
        {%- if thinking and (has_tools or loop.index0 > ns.last_user) -%}
            {{- message.get('reasoning_content', '') + '</think>' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- message['content'] or '' -}}
        {%- if message.get('tool_calls') -%}
            {{- '\n\n<' + dsml_token + 'tool_calls>\n' -}}
            {%- set tc_parts = namespace(parts=[]) -%}
            {%- for tc in message['tool_calls'] -%}
                {%- set func = tc['function'] -%}
                {%- set args = func['arguments'] -%}
                {%- if args is string -%}
                    {%- set args = args | from_json -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- set p_parts = namespace(parts=[]) -%}
                {%- for key, val in args.items() -%}
                    {%- if val is string -%}
                        {%- set _ = p_parts.parts.append('<' + dsml_token + 'parameter name="' + key + '" string="true">' + val + '</' + dsml_token + 'parameter>') -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {%- set _ = p_parts.parts.append('<' + dsml_token + 'parameter name="' + key + '" string="false">' + (val | tojson) + '</' + dsml_token + 'parameter>') -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- set _ = tc_parts.parts.append('<' + dsml_token + 'invoke name="' + func['name'] + '">\n' + (p_parts.parts | join('\n')) + '\n</' + dsml_token + 'invoke>') -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {{- (tc_parts.parts | join('\n')) + '\n</' + dsml_token + 'tool_calls>' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {{- '<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
    {%- else -%}
        {{- raise_exception('deepseek-v4 chat template: unsupported role ' + message['role']) -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
